A classic holiday potluck staple. Tender broccoli florets baked in a creamy blend of cheddar, Parmesan, mushroom soup, and Dijon mustard, crowned with a golden, buttery Ritz cracker crumb crust.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/recipes/a54972/easy-broccoli-cheese-casserole-recipe/?source=nl).*

## Ingredients

- Nonstick cooking spray
- ½ cup (1 stick) unsalted butter
- 1 can (15 oz) cream of mushroom soup
- 2 large eggs, lightly beaten
- 1 cup mayonnaise
- 2 cups shredded cheddar cheese
- ¾ cup freshly grated Parmesan cheese
- 1 tablespoon Dijon mustard
- Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste
- 1 lb. frozen chopped broccoli, defrosted and thoroughly drained
- 1 sleeve (about 1 cup) Ritz crackers, crushed
- Freshly chopped parsley, for garnish

## Instructions

1. **Preheat and Prep:** Set your oven to 350°F (175°C). Lightly grease a 9x13-inch baking dish or oval casserole dish with cooking spray.
2. **Build the Creamy Cheese Sauce:** Place a saucepan over medium-low heat and melt the stick of butter. Whisk in the condensed mushroom soup, beaten eggs, mayonnaise, grated cheddar, Parmesan, and tangy Dijon mustard. Continue whisking gently until the cheeses melt and a thick, smooth sauce forms. Season with kosher salt and ground black pepper to taste.
3. **Layer the Vegetables:** Make sure the thawed broccoli is pressed dry with a clean kitchen towel or paper towels to prevent excess water in the dish. Scatter the broccoli evenly across the bottom of the prepared casserole pan.
4. **Sauce and Crumb Topping:** Pour the warm cheese sauce over the broccoli, spreading it gently with a silicone spatula so every floret is coated. Finish by distributing the crushed Ritz crackers across the top in an even, buttery blanket.
5. **Bake Until Crisp and Bubbling:** Slide into the oven for 30 minutes. You want the cracker crust to turn toasted golden brown and the cheese sauce to simmer vigorously along the borders of the pan.
6. **Rest and Garnish:** Let the casserole sit on a trivet for 5 minutes to settle slightly. Sprinkle with minced fresh parsley and serve hot.

## Notes

- **Moisture Control:** Thawed frozen broccoli carries lots of water. Be sure to press it firmly in a colander or with paper towels before layering to keep the sauce rich rather than watery.
- **Fresh Broccoli:** You can substitute 1 lb of fresh broccoli florets; simply steam or blanch them for 3 minutes until crisp-tender before assembling.
